+// lrat-check-strict: lrat-check.c of drat-trim (commit 2e3b2dc0ecf9) with two changes, both of which only refuse more.
+// 1. Every added clause, the empty clause included, must be RUP through its hints: the hints, taken in order, end in a
+//    conflict. The original also accepted a clause with no conflict when no clause with the negated first literal was
+//    known (a pure-literal step), and that test let an empty clause with arbitrary hints through: a satisfiable CNF
+//    with the proof "3 0 0" was VERIFIED. RAT steps are not accepted either (CaDiCaL's LRAT does not need them).
+// 2. Numbers are read as decimal 64-bit values and refused outside the range of int (the original read them with
+//    %i into an int: an id of 5000000000 wrapped around, 010 was read as octal).
+#define STRICT 1
